r sharing opportunities and resources to support PSOP engagement.</p></header><section class="intro"><div class="card"><h3 style="margin-top:0;color:#001e62">Welcome to the PSOP Engagement Bulletin!</h3><p><strong>Engagement is about building community and fostering belonging.</strong></p><p>As Director of Engagement, I hope to support a welcoming community for PSOP faculty, staff, trainees, and collaborators. The monthly bulletin will serve as a resource for sharing events, programs, and opportunities across the College, University, and Community.</p></div><div class="card red"><h3 style="margin-top:0;color:#d50032">In This Bulletin</h3><ul><li><a href="#events">October Events</a></li><li><a href="#more">More Engagement Information</a></li><li><a href="#connect">Stay Connected</a></li></ul></div></section><h2 id="events">October Events</h2><p>Engagement related events across campus and the community this month.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Date / time</th><th>Event</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="date">October 10, 2026<br>11:00 AM–4:00 PM</td><td><a href="https://stumblday.com/events/indigenous-peoples-day-celebration-at-harrison-harrison-carter-park-2026-10-10">Indigenous Peoples' Day Celebration at Harrison</a><div class="meta">In-Person Event</div></td></tr><tr><td class="date">October 12, 2026<br>All Day</td><td><strong>Indigenous Peoples' Day</strong><div class="meta"></div></td></tr><tr><td class="date">October 12, 2026<br>12:30–1:20 PM</td><td><strong>Mary Moody: Keynote Speaker: Women Pharmacist Day</strong><div class="meta">In-Person or Zoom Event, see below</div></td></tr><tr><td class="date">October 15, 2026<br>11:00 AM–12:30 PM</td><td><a href="https://teaching.uic.edu/events/teaching-in-turbulent-times-uic-resources-to-support-student-well-being-2/">Teaching in Turbulent Times: UIC Resources to Support Student Well-Being</a><div class="meta">Virtual Event</div></td></tr><tr><td class="date">October 20, 2026<br>2:00–3:15 PM</td><td><a href="https://teaching.uic.edu/events/when-screens-go-silent-boosting-engagement-in-synchronous-online-learning-3/">When Screens Go Silent: Boosting Engagement in Synchronous Online Learning</a><div class="meta">Virtual Event</div></td></tr><tr><td class="date">October 21, 2026<br>2:00–4:30 PM</td><td><a href="https://nasp.uic.edu/events/fall-2026-speaker-series-w-freshwaterlab/">NASP Fall 2026 Speaker Series: Niibii Aabe Bimaadiziwaan - Water is Life in Action: Line 5 and the Great Lakes</a><div class="meta">In-Person Event</div></td></tr><tr><td class="date">October 22, 2026<br>9:00 AM–4:30 PM</td><td><a href="https://wellnesscenter.uic.edu/workshops/mental-health-first-aid/">Mental Health First Aid Certification</a><div class="meta">Virtual Event</div></td></tr><tr><td class="date">October 29, 2026<br>5:30–7:30 PM</td><td><a href="https://nasp.uic.edu/events/fall-2026-speaker-series-terrys-scaries/">NASP Fall 2026 Speaker Series: Terry's Scaries: A Night of Indigenous Horror Stories</a><div class="meta">In-Person Event</div></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="more">More Engagement Information</h2><ul class="resources"><li><strong>Women Pharmacist Day Lecture Monday 10/12</strong></li><li><a href="https://counseling.uic.edu/services/togetherall-free-anonymous-24-7-peer-support/">Togetherall - Free, Anonymous 24/7 Peer Support for Students</a><br>Togetherall is a free and anonymous peer support program that is free for all UIC students to use. It is all online for easy access and no wait lists. Togetherall is monitored by mental health professionals 24/7 to help support whatever you may need.</li><li><strong>A Myaamia Artist's Map of Chicago</strong><br>By Megan Sekulich (Miami Tribe of Oklahoma)<br><br>Chicago is, and has always been, an Indigenous place. Using the waterways of šikaakonki ‘Chicago’ and northern Illinois as an outline, the space between each river is filled with native flora and fauna, many of which are culturally significant to myaamiaki ‘Myaamia people’.<br><br>Megan also created a linework-only version of the graphic as a coloring activity, which you can <a href="https://indigenous-chicago.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/storymap-v4-lines-1-scaled.jpg">download here</a>.</li></ul><h2 id="connect">Stay Connected</h2><p>Feel free to let me know of any Engagement related news, events, or updates to share in a future bulletin!</p><p>– Taylor</p></div><footer class="footer"><strong>Pharmacy Systems, Outcomes and Policy</strong><br>Retzky College of Pharmacy | University of Illinois Chicago</footer><div class="ai-ack" style="font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:11px;line-height:1.4;color:#6b7280;text-align:center;padding:14px 22px;background:#f6f8fb;"><strong>AI Acknowledgment:</strong> Generative AI was used to assist with formatting and web development. Content was created, compiled, and reviewed by Taylor.</div></main></body></html>
